<div class="mw-parser-output"><h1>Eagle Cry</h1>
<p>Sphere: Summoning Sphere
Class: Ranger (guild level 29, up to 50%)
Mana: 20
</p><p>Usage:
</p>
<pre><a cmd='#'>cast eagle cry</a>
</pre>
<p>The ranger calls out into the sky 'aquila!', and an eagle swoops down out 
of nowhere and alights on the ranger's shoulder. It follows you, and fights 
for you by itself: when you fight, it attacks your foe, and when your 
wounds grow serious, below a third of your hit points, it tries to rescue 
you. It does no harm to another player unless both of you have signed the 
Book of Blood. You can give it orders with tell, for example 'tell eagle 
kill orc'.
</p><p>The eagle stays only a short while, from twenty seconds to a little over a 
minute, the better your spell, and then flies away, its mission fulfilled. 
Banish sends it away sooner. It needs the open sky: indoors, or wherever 
the weather doesn't reach, the spell can't be cast. You must be standing, 
not fighting. Practising it needs divine 58. It is also found on scrolls.
</p><p><br />
See Also:
</p>
<pre>&gt; <a cmd='#'>Help Summon Animal</a>
&gt; <a cmd='#'>Help Banish</a>
&gt; <a cmd='#'>Help Summoning Sphere</a>
</pre>




</div>